#{[{:activity/expected-seconds 720.0 :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189169} :activity/id #uuid "2c1b60fe-19a1-5c76-8d58-a10c1ae4790c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049871 :topic/id #uuid "19e888aa-f28d-5a3a-a27d-2fb784b182ea" :topic/math-academy-id 3926} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189167 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188327 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188034 :question/id #uuid "6cdc2b0e-a968-5d95-8fb6-5d469a5920b9" :question/math-academy-id "e-10302"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c80ef8f-1073-5e41-bec3-860209a731bd" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048872} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050327}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188634} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188635} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527927} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527950} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527966} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527976} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542114}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Given a Conditional Mass Function"} :step/id #uuid "2ef086e9-8163-573e-9575-a78051c9420a" :step/math-academy-id 38837 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189183}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189168 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188328 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188035 :question/id #uuid "49a039ae-dbe1-5faa-a9a7-014bd9549c03" :question/math-academy-id "e-10306"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92a52324-627c-5796-bc4f-ddeb5380f129" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188637} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188689} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186411869} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511491} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511582} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527937} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527963} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542174}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Column Totals"} :step/id #uuid "ac37dad4-4109-5b6c-a2d0-f6c46e058597" :step/math-academy-id 38849} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189169 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189401 :tutorial/content "Suppose that $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables, where the conditional expected value of $X$ given $Y=y$ is given by $\\mu_{X|y}.$ In other words,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] = \\mu_{X|y}.\n$$\n\nThe **conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$** is defined as\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] = \\textrm{E}\\big[(X - \\mu_{X|y} \\big)^2 \\,|\\, Y=y].\n$$\n\nThis is similar to the definition of $\\textrm{Var}[X]$ in that it represents the average  (squared) distance of the random variable $X$ from the mean. The difference here is that the expected values are now dependent on the outcome of $Y.$\n\nSimilarly to the case of $\\textrm{Var}[X],$ this often isn't the easiest formula to use in practice. However, it can be shown that the definition of conditional variance is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $f_{X|Y}(x \\,|\\, y)$ is the conditional PMF of $X$ given $Y.$ Note that these formulas are analogous to those for $\\textrm{Var}[X].$\n\nFinally, we have an analogous definition for the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "ce4fb1c3-94ee-51c3-b10d-ce6ea0c7ff38" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6431 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "12bb1f79-4af3-56c1-b495-e654c2cf5d1c" :step/math-academy-id 38850 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189167}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189183 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188339 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188046 :question/id #uuid "3764cb54-7fd2-584a-9dc7-eda88368b032" :question/math-academy-id "e-10352"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abfaf356-6b74-5dfd-8070-e3a60dc372c5" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188680} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188687} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511456} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511574} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527926} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527932} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527968} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542228}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Conditional Variance Using Row Totals"} :step/id #uuid "7f447a96-6d58-5356-934d-4d4a94738359" :step/math-academy-id 38984 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186189168}}] :activity/title "Conditional Variance for Discrete Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186188511}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511586} :activity/id #uuid "2295589f-1938-53e1-a9aa-ded9c732eec7" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049871 :topic/id #uuid "19e888aa-f28d-5a3a-a27d-2fb784b182ea" :topic/math-academy-id 3926} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511586 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511456 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ec68043-b866-5e5b-8bb7-32d1408e60c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510927} {:answer/id #uuid "c5e9e267-a7b8-546e-8ca5-7597e4f9d784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511189} {:answer/id #uuid "e38c50ad-e0fc-52f2-b45a-0aed3bf8753b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511255} {:answer/id #uuid "e3a0e51e-a2b2-5d25-84bb-27f6878f5ff2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511256} {:answer/id #uuid "e3c50614-2143-5835-91a2-26951415d4a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511259}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511259} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e701f23-45b5-584b-9ff7-052c5c629f38" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "047bb67d-8c03-57ec-a81f-c32911be6893" :question/math-academy-id "q-146226" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ | $\\frac{7}{27}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=0]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|0}=2.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ | $\\frac{16}{27}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ | $\\frac{7}{27}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{11}{27}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{9}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{11}$ | $\\frac{7}{11}$ | $\\frac{3}{11}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=0] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)]-{\\mu }_{Y|0}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{9}{16}+{4}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{8}+{8}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{16}]-{2}^{2} \\\\  & =0+6+4-4 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0300a9fc-85df-55bb-885b-ea046fb4bb5e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511666}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511606 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511574 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46451ad3-292e-5818-b57f-512919c1b762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510940} {:answer/id #uuid "85f1ae38-1f12-5af1-9e47-1e397e55e732" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511058} {:answer/id #uuid "9848b01d-ae3d-5b11-a03c-4137d1ec2d54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511099} {:answer/id #uuid "e44fbbd6-2948-5df7-8863-f9b14dba4caa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511260} {:answer/id #uuid "f1966108-9bd3-50ba-ae71-0b6fda1b9652" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511278}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511260} :answer-field/id #uuid "273fb450-78e1-578c-ad1c-ea60b9f9611a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511330}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e9ff9199-1184-598e-a945-b789f3d5b0b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-146236" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=5$ | $Y=10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{25}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{25}$ | $\\frac{1}{25}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=6]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|6}=\\frac{15}{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=5$ | $Y=10$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{25}$ | $\\frac{23}{25}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{25}$ | $\\frac{1}{25}$ | $\\frac{2}{25}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=5$ | $Y=10$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{20}{23}$ | $\\frac{3}{23}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=6] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,6)]-{\\mu }_{Y|6}^{2} \\\\  & =[{5}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{10}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}]-{(\\frac{15}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{2}+50-\\frac{225}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{25}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "30c58b82-3c11-5385-abbd-de1c4e8158be" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511670}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511621 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511582 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14738cb2-b471-5d99-b3eb-4afbb5fa348a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510824} {:answer/id #uuid "20ae5337-49f2-5726-8ce9-b5fca604cf7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510853} {:answer/id #uuid "518547db-16ad-50af-8a24-b4267aa35a9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510957} {:answer/id #uuid "a50bc467-b427-559a-829c-9f60582a46c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511128} {:answer/id #uuid "ee546c20-c60e-59e8-af15-1c8202fb7fba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511274}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510824} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f312ee4-2cb7-5564-9f11-50b74da2484d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511318}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "fa585366-16bd-5221-b5b1-a80000ac4783" :question/math-academy-id "q-146282" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|2}=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)]-{\\mu }_{X|2}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}]-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{2}+1-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "54fc286d-ca29-5168-94f4-61b515ef6f44"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511666 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188687 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f4abe7f7-40a7-5fee-8c26-2ce6a49da4ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186403} {:answer/id #uuid "02c37c21-5706-5110-839d-3b7f23f1c8c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186404} {:answer/id #uuid "28522e3b-eba5-534c-bcd9-5ef42a50ee9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186405} {:answer/id #uuid "42159274-25fc-5902-8f54-b1273ec708fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{11}{25}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186406} {:answer/id #uuid "56837666-e2e8-5a77-9c5c-5bd3b0c1b2ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186407}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186186403} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b741eef-9c5a-588c-9901-de8a736211a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e6e8480d-863e-574b-98a7-52fe067fa786" :question/math-academy-id "q-146230" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=\\frac{6}{5}.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{5}{8}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =[{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{5}+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}]-{(\\frac{6}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{36}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d245c012-0e70-5d3b-bb3f-3e7de5fe0a63" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511606}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511670 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511491 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66d1570e-0fc2-5b26-944e-0848dd40f138" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510998} {:answer/id #uuid "7e4bbbd8-2767-5014-b1ea-d2f03b69e408" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511040} {:answer/id #uuid "82fe3a83-b24a-5a3c-bffb-cf8e5344fd6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511051} {:answer/id #uuid "9f3745f3-2e12-5887-955e-9fd687c8f6c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511116} {:answer/id #uuid "b3aef80f-ba63-5a2a-892f-31618b540913" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511153}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511153} :answer-field/id #uuid "798593a5-cfe0-5f7d-84fa-43e7795c761a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186511372}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4b9363aa-00d2-51a2-9bff-045f9cb8f2d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-146278" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|2}=5.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{5}{16}$ | $\\frac{5}{16}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{5}$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{3}{5}$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)]-{\\mu }_{X|2}^{2} \\\\  & =[{3}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}+{9}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}]-{5}^{2} \\\\  & =6+27-25 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "dba60abd-e9be-5c2c-86c8-da39dba6d99b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186511621}}] :activity/title "Conditional Variance for Discrete Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186510755}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046660} :activity/first-step {:db/id 