lue is ${\\mu }_{X|9}=\\frac{9}{7}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{10}{27}$ | $\\frac{5}{27}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{27}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{7}{27}$ | $\\frac{13}{27}$ | $\\frac{7}{27}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{6}{7}$ | $\\frac{10}{13}$ | $\\frac{5}{7}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{7}$ | $\\frac{3}{13}$ | $\\frac{2}{7}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=9] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,9)]-{\\mu }_{X|9}^{2} \\\\  & =[{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{7}+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{7}]-{(\\frac{9}{7})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{7}+\\frac{8}{7}-\\frac{81}{49} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{49}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "2efcbc03-ec16-5aa6-be91-e8353500b6fd" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542262}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542251 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542114 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ad02fa8-3481-5a35-8f97-e44b965d8aa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.08" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541477} {:answer/id #uuid "9edb3ba8-6472-5571-8e40-1e3dfa7a1e0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541754} {:answer/id #uuid "b28d688f-5c4d-53f7-89d3-91e51d6d25a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541789} {:answer/id #uuid "b7eefa51-6fa1-53f2-a256-4865ca5dfa9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541801} {:answer/id #uuid "cfd19712-7a9f-5b0a-9bd8-01f5e442e63d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "1.38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541863}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541789} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d904fdd-21aa-5b06-aab9-981bfbc03271" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "0a174da3-b391-5e95-bb6f-67313dad4a2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-146203" :question/problem "| $x$ | $1$ | $2$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ | $0.3$ | $0.45$ | $0.25$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ is shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|2}=2.2.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)]-{\\mu }_{X|2}^{2} \\\\  & =[(1)^{2}\\cdot 0.3+(2)^{2}\\cdot 0.45+(4)^{2}\\cdot 0.25]-(2.2)^{2} \\\\  & =0.3+1.8+4-4.84 \\\\  & =1.26.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "456c9817-f9b5-5e02-ad7e-aba7476b75ff" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542261}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542261 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542228 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16d692bd-0e74-560a-a96c-8d8461608311" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541468} {:answer/id #uuid "74a88296-9ddf-544e-9d53-a64399f2a11a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541663} {:answer/id #uuid "9267e4c1-e2af-5f31-bbf9-2d596a42e1d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541723} {:answer/id #uuid "b4ff7745-61b1-5fe6-ad1b-f5ee14b3580b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541795} {:answer/id #uuid "e265f954-217e-5676-a722-342362e50106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541902}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541468} :answer-field/id #uuid "ebb5d8b0-09a9-5d9e-8e09-86d97b61cdf1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186542089}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f6596362-8154-5a9b-b6ee-af9895a85a60" :question/math-academy-id "q-146227" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=2]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|2}=1.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=2] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)]-{\\mu }_{Y|2}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}+{2}^{2}\\cdot 0+{4}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}]-{1}^{2} \\\\  & =0+0+4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "71644673-4b60-52c3-b90a-66ca26f88cd7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542245}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542262 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542174 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e4f18e3-c2c7-5633-ad51-327c11dda76f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{29}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541451} {:answer/id #uuid "1742151a-fdad-55b5-83cf-1eac826f3b6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541470} {:answer/id #uuid "6fb12aa8-c236-5848-bf31-4b538dca5489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{17}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541648} {:answer/id #uuid "b235bce1-5f22-5ec4-b929-1a8d2bf6ab80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{40}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541788} {:answer/id #uuid "f97c1141-ae12-5ca0-8969-0f2ba9d5bac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{38}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541945}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541945} :answer-field/id #uuid "2224a384-1d96-5035-96d8-8e3991487107" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541979}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9a9df102-8e4d-542b-ad62-072cc2469e7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-146287" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{5}{27}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=3]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|3}=\\frac{22}{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{27}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{5}{27}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=3$ | $Y=9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| $X=6$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{6}$ |\n| $X=9$ | $\\frac{5}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=3] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,3)]-{\\mu }_{X|3}^{2} \\\\  & =[{3}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{9}+{6}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}+{9}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{5}{9}]-{(\\frac{22}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1+12+45-\\frac{484}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{38}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "76632a42-7076-5678-bdc5-b59bab16ce2a"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542277 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186188680 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b20165e2-6fe7-54aa-8006-6fcf097ac4fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186361} {:answer/id #uuid "d91ffcfa-8adc-595a-b349-50d0122ff2db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186362} {:answer/id #uuid "f9187b5e-22bc-5d31-abd4-265dd8a9df03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186363} {:answer/id #uuid "2b8a778f-9674-5eb0-98b5-530ecc1f069f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186364} {:answer/id #uuid "34075399-76f6-5159-a3eb-3e2a37a1ff99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186365}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186186363} :answer-field/id #uuid "6762d125-e9d7-5f02-9226-4a00e4721756" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186186360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "60cb8cd8-f4a1-51b2-afe3-57e452f5f729" :question/math-academy-id "q-146159" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=0]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|0}=1.$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=0] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|0}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}+{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}+{2}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}]-{(1)}^{2} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{2}+1-1 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ccfd8164-083c-5eef-a333-3dcb0ae83dcf" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186542251}}] :activity/title "Conditional Variance for Discrete Random Variables" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541422}]}
